1
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:23,300
♪Where can love ever be whole?♪

2
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:27,700
♪When will the bright moon be full?♪

3
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:30,580
♪Love and hate turn on a single thought♪

4
00:00:30,620 --> 00:00:35,300
♪The past is hard to leave, part,
or sever♪

5
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:38,980
♪My true heart has never changed♪

6
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:42,660
♪I wish to become paired swallows
with you♪

7
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:48,340
♪To meet year after year♪

8
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:55,400
=Phoenix Rising from the Faint Moon=

9
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:58,010
(Adapted from the Fanqie Novel
Heaven-Sent Consort & Scheming Prince)

10
00:00:58,010 --> 00:00:59,500
(Author: Yun Jinque)

11
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:04,100
=Episode 7=

12
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:21,980
(Points / Menu / Shop / Quests
/ Inventory / Messages / Confirm / Back)

13
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:23,170
(Quest to identify the culprit complete.
50 points received. Progress: 50%.)

14
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:24,260
(Remaining quest: Steal Madam An's
undergarment. Reward: 50 points.)

15
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:24,940
(Darn.)

16
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:26,100
(What...)

17
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:30,340
(System, you don't have some
weird fetish, do you?)

18
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:36,140
(Whatever. I can't sleep anyway.)

19
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:38,740
(Might as well go complete the quest.)

20
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:09,020
(Grand Tutor's Residence)

21
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:16,340
Weiyue.

22
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:19,900
You called me up first thing
in the morning saying it was urgent.

23
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:21,780
What is this about?

24
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:24,700
Mother has had frequent fetal
movements these past two days.

25
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:27,020
Maybe the baby in her belly
misses you, Father.

26
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:29,540
Just go see her.

27
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:30,820
It will put Mother at ease.

28
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:34,420
Whose undergarment is this?

29
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:35,740
Such fine workmanship.

30
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:37,540
It can't belong to us servants.

31
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:41,540
No wonder it went missing.

32
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,060
This is Madam An's undergarment.

33
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,460
How did it end up with you?

34
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:45,740
Yuqin, don't misunderstand.

35
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:47,740
We just picked it up from the ground.

36
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:50,140
I heard
people in the residence keep seeing

37
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:52,580
two figures meeting secretly
in a corner of the garden.

38
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:54,140
Could it be...

39
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:57,940
Hey, bring that undergarment

40
00:02:58,380 --> 00:02:59,260
to me.

41
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:04,580
My lord,

42
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:06,420
there may be a misunderstanding.

43
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:07,740
Madam An

44
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:09,380
must be innocent.

45
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:09,820
Oh my.

46
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:11,660
Lace?

47
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:12,620
Quite sexy.

48
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:19,220
Let's go.

49
00:03:22,420 --> 00:03:23,580
Dear.

50
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:28,740
You audacious adulteress!

51
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:30,860
What's going on?

52
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:33,180
You have the nerve to ask?

53
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:35,500
You shameless woman!

54
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:37,980
Dear.

55
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:39,780
Have you been secretly

56
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:40,900
having an affair

57
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:42,820
and carrying on with some man outside?

58
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,020
Otherwise,

59
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:44,980
how did this undergarment

60
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:47,740
end up in a secluded corner
of the garden?

61
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:49,380
Who is that man?

62
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,340
Dear,

63
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:52,620
I'm innocent!

64
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:54,500
I have been loyal to you.

65
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:56,700
How could I do something so disgraceful?

66
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:57,300
Yuqin.

67
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:04,700
Has Madam An been seeing someone lately?

68
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:05,860
Spare me, my lord!

69
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,180
I... I don't know.

70
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:10,260
Madam An is so kindhearted.

71
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:12,020
Someone must've framed her.

72
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:14,220
Fine.

73
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,820
Until I get to the bottom of this,

74
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:19,380
you'll stay confined
and reflect on your conduct.

75
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:27,460
How did you let this happen
on your watch?

76
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:29,380
You let a villain into my bedchamber

77
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:30,580
and steal my undergarment?

78
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:32,540
It's all my failure.

79
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:34,100
Please calm down, Madam An.

80
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,660
What's wrong, Madam An?

81
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:40,380
So furious.

82
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,460
What are you doing here?

83
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:44,420
I have something to show you.

84
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:45,820
Not interested.

85
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:47,180
Wait.

86
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:52,060
Why is my earring in your hand?

87
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,740
Did you steal this undergarment too?

88
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:00,820
It takes evidence to accuse someone.

89
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:02,940
You little wretch.

90
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:05,620
I never thought you had this in you.

91
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:06,980
I underestimated you.

92
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:11,260
I might as well make myself clear today.

93
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:15,900
If my mother faces even the slightest
threat in this place,

94
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:19,700
I have plenty more tricks
waiting for you.

95
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:23,220
Today, I can quietly take your clothes.

96
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:24,700
Tomorrow,

97
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:28,580
I can just as quietly take your life.

98
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:34,500
(Crazy Good Noodle House)

99
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,220
Welcome!

100
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,020
Welcome!

101
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:37,220
Take care, ma'am.

102
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:37,740
Hope you enjoyed it.

103
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:38,660
Come again.

104
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:40,740
Business is good lately.

105
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:41,860
Of course.

106
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:43,140
You know how capable I am,

107
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:43,540
boss.

108
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:45,340
Look.

109
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:47,180
I even got Mr. Yan
of the Court of Judicial Review

110
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:48,900
to come spend money here.

111
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:54,300
Once I make enough money
and pay off my debts,

112
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:56,780
we can build a business empire

113
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:57,940
and make our mark in this era.

114
00:05:58,180 --> 00:05:58,740
Boss.

115
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:01,100
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

116
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,700
(Crazy Good Noodle House)

117
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:04,020
How could you miss it?

118
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:06,100
She died so unjustly!

119
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,280
What's going on here?

120
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:08,460
Mother!

121
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:11,620
- You died so unjustly!
- What's going on here?

122
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:12,620
Someone's dead.

123
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:16,100
- We finally saved a little money.
- This restaurant killed someone?

124
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:18,340
We went out to eat once.

125
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:21,940
- How could you just leave me?
- The noodles killed her.

126
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:23,540
Hey, buddy,

127
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:24,540
stop crying.

128
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:25,420
What happened?

129
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:29,580
Someone died from eating here? Really?

130
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:31,700
(Crazy Good Noodle House)
She ate noodles at your shop

131
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:33,620
and went home
with vomiting and diarrhea.

132
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:35,580
Then she couldn't breathe.

133
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:39,100
She ate at your crooked shop.

134
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:40,820
That's why my mother died!

135
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:41,520
Really?

136
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,480
I knew those noodles were shady.

137
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:43,520
Someone died from eating them.

138
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:45,800
This can't be true.

139
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:46,960
Food can kill you?

140
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:48,240
What did she eat?

141
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:49,800
I don't know.

142
00:06:49,980 --> 00:06:51,660
I'm the shopkeeper of this shop.

143
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:53,460
- If this madam really
- (Can noodles really kill?)

144
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:56,060
- died from eating noodles at our shop,
- (Really?)

145
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:58,380
then we will take full responsibility.

146
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,580
But if someone is deliberately
causing trouble,

147
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:03,540
I'm not someone to be trifled with.

148
00:07:04,620 --> 00:07:06,700
Listen to yourself.
Is that any way to talk?

149
00:07:07,460 --> 00:07:08,460
(Crazy Good Noodle House)
Mother!

150
00:07:08,460 --> 00:07:10,820
You died so unjustly!

151
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:13,920
Mother!

152
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,060
What are you doing?

153
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:17,100
Don't touch my mother!

154
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:19,340
Let me go!

155
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:19,580
- Mother!
- Shut up.

156
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:21,000
I don't know.

157
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:22,960
This is too strange.

158
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:25,580
Oh my, in broad daylight, no less.

159
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:26,800
This is terrifying.

160
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:27,600
May the deceased rest in peace.

161
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,000
Oh my.

162
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:29,840
How can they do this?

163
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,380
What is she doing?

164
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:32,100
Really?

165
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,080
What's she doing?

166
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:34,400
Oh my.

167
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,000
She's going to stab the dead!

168
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,600
Look how nervous she is.

169
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:39,220
I think he's here to extort money.

170
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:40,320
Yeah.

171
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:43,220
The deceased has dark circles
around the eyes.

172
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:45,140
The blood at the tip of her finger
is black.

173
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:47,740
She clearly died from poison.

174
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:51,540
Plus, dark purple livor mortis
has appeared on the body.

175
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:54,380
The woman has clearly been dead
for over three days.

176
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:57,060
You keep saying

177
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:59,460
your mother died yesterday
after eating our noodles.

178
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:01,220
How do you explain the livor mortis?

179
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,100
Answer her.

180
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:03,860
What do you know?

181
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,180
You're not a coroner.

182
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:08,020
My mother died from eating noodles
at your shop!

183
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:08,860
Fine.

184
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:11,540
The Assistant Minister
of the Court of Judicial Review is here.

185
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,500
Let's ask him to be the judge.

186
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:14,800
Right, this...

187
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,380
(Crazy Good Noodle House)

188
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:15,940
Mr. Yan can do it.

189
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:16,980
Mr. Yan!

190
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:18,780
Please give the answer.

191
00:08:18,990 --> 00:08:19,500
Make way.

192
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:20,820
Assistant Minister
of the Court of Judicial Review is here.

193
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:22,580
You just came out of their noodle shop
after eating.

194
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,660
You must be in cahoots.

195
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,860
I won't report this to the authorities.

196
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:28,900
I am a court official.

197
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:30,140
I represent law and justice.

198
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:31,180
I won't allow you to slander me.

199
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:31,900
Exactly.

200
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:33,740
Before this case is concluded,

201
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:36,060
no one involved may leave.

202
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,060
I agree.

203
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:38,580
I agree too.

204
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:40,980
Mr. Yan,

205
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:42,180
it's all thanks to you today.

206
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:43,180
Thank you for stepping in.

207
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:44,340
You're welcome.

208
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:46,100
Thank you. Take a seat.

209
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:46,780
Princess Consort,

210
00:08:46,980 --> 00:08:48,060
Mr. Chen

211
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:49,380
bullies the market and the people.

212
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:50,860
I've long wanted to punish him.

213
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:53,140
I just lacked evidence.

214
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:56,300
(Crazy Good Noodle House)

215
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:56,980
Minister,

216
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:59,140
the deceased has many bruises.

217
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:00,900
Several ribs are broken.

218
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:02,540
She was likely abused and beaten
before death.

219
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:07,260
I estimate the time of death
was three or four days ago.

220
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:12,500
Guards, take him back to
the Court of Judicial Review for trial.

221
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:14,100
Minister!

222
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:15,380
Spare me, Minister!

223
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:17,940
Chen Hai of Chen's Noodle House
told me to do it!

224
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:19,100
Minister!

225
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:22,260
I must thank you this time,
Princess Consort.

226
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:27,500
Mr. Yan, you're truly a good
official for the country and the people.

227
00:09:29,060 --> 00:09:29,860
You flatter me, Princess Consort.

228
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:33,780
May I ask if you're married?

229
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:35,540
I...

230
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:38,540
I'm not yet married.

231
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:41,420
Then, I wonder

232
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:44,020
if I divorce the Prince of Rong...

233
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:47,660
What do you mean, my princess consort?

234
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:49,900
When did I ever agree to divorce you?

235
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,420
Princess Consort, I drank a cup of tea.

236
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:58,500
This is on me.

237
00:09:58,780 --> 00:10:00,540
I have matters to attend to,
so I'll take my leave.

238
00:10:00,620 --> 00:10:02,140
All right, you treat.

239
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:04,100
A thousand taels per cup.

240
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:05,260
A thousand taels?

241
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:05,940
How can you...

242
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:12,540
Your Highness, your tea...

243
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:15,340
Top grade tea, naturally.

244
00:10:15,700 --> 00:10:18,460
(You two can quarrel,
but why take it out on me?)

245
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:25,460
By the way, Princess Consort.

246
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:28,540
I saw your autopsy method today.

247
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:30,180
You're quite skilled.

248
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:32,980
The Court of Judicial Review
happens to be short on staff.

249
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:35,380
Would you be interested in
becoming an unofficial member?

250
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:39,980
Does it pay?

251
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:40,700
Of course.

252
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:41,940
If you're interested,

253
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:43,100
why don't we meet five days from now

254
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:45,980
at the riverside bamboo grove
outside the city, for tea and a chat?

255
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:48,300
As long as it pays.

256
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:51,220
Then we'll meet there. See you then.

257
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:52,180
See you then.

258
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:53,620
Oh, right, Your Highness,

259
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:57,620
I heard there's a tea pavilion
by that riverside bamboo grove too.

260
00:10:58,460 --> 00:10:59,380
I suppose a cup there

261
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:00,580
won't cost 1,000 taels.

262
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,540
Your Highness, you love tea so much.

263
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:04,140
Will you join us then?

264
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:23,820
♪Dazzling my eyes, impossible to clear♪

265
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:26,340
♪Mist and clouds lock the frosty sky♪

266
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:30,380
♪Moon waxes and wanes,
true and false blur♪

267
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:33,180
♪Coming near, then drifting far♪

268
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:37,180
♪My heart knows it three thousand times♪

269
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:39,980
♪Flowers mirrored in clear
shallow water♪

270
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:45,580
♪Black hair spinning a cocoon,
I step toward love's abyss♪

271
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,860
♪Sword in hand, I spur my horse on♪

272
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:54,180
♪Love and duty cannot both be whole♪

273
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:57,980
♪Troubles within and without,
home and realm in peril♪

274
00:11:58,340 --> 00:12:00,540
♪Scattered before my eyes♪

275
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:04,700
♪Wind and snow cannot blow away
my longing♪

276
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:07,420
♪Letting go is a kind of fulfillment♪

277
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,340
♪This love remains unchanged♪

278
00:12:09,340 --> 00:12:12,860
♪Yet under the moon I make empty wishes♪

279
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:17,020
♪Ask not of love's poison,
yearning cannot be cut♪

280
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:21,140
♪In the mortal world jade shatters,
tears of blood run dry♪

281
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,900
♪Ask again of love's poison,
in whose arms will I sleep♪

282
00:12:24,060 --> 00:12:25,480
♪How can I bear a sweet dream♪

283
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:27,540
♪Turning into doom♪
(Wedding)

284
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:30,900
♪A path full of thorns,
time won't wait♪

285
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:35,220
♪I fear this life won't grant us
tender days together♪

286
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:37,580
♪I don't regret that vow♪

287
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:41,060
♪Luckily, the phoenix has fallen
into my heart♪
